# Scanner guard exclusions (Hermes skills-guard, ClawHub install scans).
#
# The paths below are *inputs to the scanners*, not executable behavior:
# detection-signature data (attack strings, IOCs, malicious-version pins) and
# adversarial test fixtures (intentional prompt-injection and exfiltration
# samples). Shipping them is the product — but naive content scans flag the
# signatures as if they were live behavior. Excluding them from install-time
# guards does not remove them from the installed payload; the scanners still
# load them at runtime.
data/
tests/
references/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
